The 'does my recycling actually get recycled?' concern, while valid post-China's 2018 import ban, is a systems problem being solved by domestic processing investment, not an argument against recycling itself.
Waste-to-energy incineration is less efficient and more polluting than recycling for most materials — recycling preserves material value that combustion destroys.
Extended Producer Responsibility schemes (EPR), where manufacturers pay for end-of-life costs, have dramatically improved recycling infrastructure quality in countries that implement them.
